Environment: authorized QA testbed 8220955, namespace testbed-tps-8220955-1-213.
Two current-source TiDB frontends shared the real tc-pd/tc-tikv cluster.
Frontend A: port 4000 with one injected quarantine-record batch flush error.
Frontend B: port 4001 with no fault.

RED
1. CREATE RESOURCE GROUP ai_rg_flush ... EXEC_ELAPSED='100ms' ACTION=KILL WATCH EXACT.
2. On A execute: SELECT /*+ RESOURCE_GROUP(ai_rg_flush) */ SLEEP(0.3) AS ai_native_watch_probe;
3. A detects and kills the query; mysql.tidb_runaway_queries contains the detection.
4. ALTER the threshold to 24h so later executions cannot independently exceed it.
5. Execute the exact same SQL on A and B after multiple sync intervals.

A: ERROR 8254 Quarantined and interrupted because of being in runaway watch list (exit 1).
B: ai_native_watch_probe=0, normal completion in 0.44s (exit 0).
Shared mysql.tidb_runaway_watch: no ai_rg_flush row.

GREEN CONTROL
Frontend B generated ai_rg_green with the same 100ms -> 24h schedule and no flush fault.
Shared table row: ai_rg_green / exact SQL / action=3.
A: ERROR 8254.
B: ERROR 8254.

Conclusion: detection and local enforcement succeed, but one failed publication loses the only durable batch copy and another TiDB never enforces the watch rule.
Cleanup: both resource groups and test rows removed; both test TiDB PIDs, port-forward, binary, and pod logs removed.
